# 7 Check-in step by step (v6 slide 12)
"""[7:15 - 9:15]  KEY MESSAGE: a visit only counts when the rep is really there, and every visit brings back shelf data.
This is the check-in, step by step.
The rep opens the customer and taps Check In. The phone finds the GPS position at once.
The check-in is accepted only within 300 metres of the outlet, and the real distance and the GPS accuracy are saved with it. So a visit report from the office or from the car is not possible.
Then he chooses what happened: order placed, payment collected, assortment check, delivery or a revisit.
Then comes the part that matters most for you: the shelf. He records whether Castrol is available, whether the full range is there, and whether there is fake product. And he ticks the competitor brands he sees on the shelf.
He adds a short note and a photo, in high resolution when he wants to capture the price tags, and submits.
It works without signal, which matters in basements and in the regions. If an order was placed, the order screen opens straight away.
For a team lead, the important point is this: you no longer manage the team by asking where they were. You can see it, and you can spend your time on what they found.""",

