# 21 AI agent (v6 slide 25)
"""[25:15 - 27:00]  KEY MESSAGE: the AI agent is a team lead that never forgets.
This is our AI agent. In the app we call him Vaghinak.
He watches the working day: late starts, missed visits, long stays in the office.
He keeps visits on route: he reminds reps about planned shops nearby.
He chases money: overdue debt, down payments and broken promises.
He gives each task to the right person with a deadline, and the task closes by itself when the problem is solved, for example when the payment arrives.
Some of his questions must be answered before the rep carries on, and management only hears about what slips.
On the left is the management view, on the right the rep's view. He talks to each person in their own tone: formal with management, friendly with the reps.
Look at the management view: an evening message like "Rep B started 41 minutes late, the third time this week; Rep C stopped after 4 of 9 planned visits". And on the rep's side: "Nice work today. There are two planned shops 200 metres from your last stop. Will you drop in before you leave the area?"
For a team lead in this room, think of him as an assistant who follows up on every outlet, every day, and who never forgets.""",

# 22 How the AI agent decides (v6 slide 26)
"""[27:00 - 28:45]  KEY MESSAGE: watch, notice, assign, check, escalate.
How does he decide? Five steps. He watches the data the app collects all day: orders, payments, visits and check-ins. He notices when something differs from the usual pattern of a customer or a rep. He assigns a task to the right person, with a deadline. He checks the data to see whether it was done, and closes the task by himself. And he escalates to management only when it keeps slipping.
Three examples. A customer usually orders every two weeks, and this time no order came. The agent gives the rep a task to visit and remind the customer, and the task closes when the next order arrives. For the brand, that is a lost order saved.
A customer pays every week, and this week there is no payment. The agent creates a task to collect it, and when the rep records the money on the customer card, the task closes by itself.
And the team starts the day at the office. When someone arrives late, the agent asks for the reason, and after the third time management is told.
The pattern is always the same: the agent notices early, gives a clear task to one person, and checks the result in the data. Nobody has to remember to follow up.""",

